abstract: >-
  EEGSynthesizer is a stochastic parametric synthesizer of scalp EEG
  signals with physiologically coherent ictal morphology. It generates
  large-scale synthetic datasets of virtual patients (3,000 patients,
  19-channel 10-20 montage, 250 Hz) covering two epileptic phenotypes:
  generalized absence seizures and focal temporal seizures. The framework
  is designed to address the scarcity of labeled ictal EEG data by
  producing training sets transferable to the real clinical domain,
  validated against the CHB-MIT Scalp EEG Dataset (PhysioNet). Signal
  generation models 1/f background noise, spike-wave patterns (2.4–4.2
  Hz), inter-channel spatial correlation via common field mixing, and
  realistic artifacts (eye blinks, EMG, non-ictal confounders). The
  pipeline includes five cross-validation protocols: internal
  separability, Real-to-Real (R2R), Synthetic-to-Real (TSTR),
  Real-to-Synthetic (TRTS), and augmentation. The synthesizer is part of
  a doctoral thesis in biomedical engineering targeting Q1 publication.

